    "message": "Add Kimi K2.5 MXFP4 vLLM benchmark for MI355X + bug temp patches due to vllm #35641 #35633 (#825)\n\n* Add Kimi K2.5 MXFP4 vLLM benchmark for MI355X (TP8)\n\n- Add kimik2.5-fp4-mi355x-vllm config to amd-master.yaml\n  - Model: amd/Kimi-K2.5-MXFP4\n  - Image: vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:v0.15.1\n  - TP=8, concurrency 4-64 for 1k1k, 1k8k, 8k1k\n- Add benchmark script benchmarks/single_node/kimik2.5_fp4_mi355x.sh\n- Update perf-changelog.yaml\n\nCloses #824\n\nCo-authored-by: functionstackx <functionstackx@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update amd-master.yaml\n\n* Update amd-master.yaml\n\n* Add pip install amd-quark for MXFP4 quantization support\n\nThe amd-quark package is required by vLLM to dequantize MXFP4 models.\nWithout it, the server fails with ImportError during model loading.\n\nCo-authored-by: functionstackx <functionstackx@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Add VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 env var for AMD AIter kernels\n\nCo-authored-by: functionstackx <functionstackx@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Remove VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 env var (AITER doesn't support TP8 Kimi K2.5 MLA)\n\nAITER MLA only supports 16 or 128 number of heads, but TP8 Kimi K2.5\nprovides 8 heads, causing an AssertionError at runtime.\n\nCo-authored-by: functionstackx <functionstackx@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Increase benchmark template timeout from 4 hours to 5 hours\n\nCo-authored-by: functionstackx <functionstackx@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* add descriptions of the bugs & link issues\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: claude[bot] <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: functionstackx <functionstackx@users.noreply.github.com>",
